course: dictionary
lesson: 10169
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. The dictionary gives tick several meanings. Read the words around it first. «The teacher put a tick next to each right answer.» The words right answer show that a tick here is a mark, not a sound or an insect.
explain: «The clock gave a loud tick every second.» Clock, every second and loud are your clues, so this tick is a sound. Tick can also be a verb, as in «tick the box», which means to make a mark.
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Check your skin after a walk in long grass, because a tick can bite.» Skin, grass and bite tell you a tick is a tiny creature here, not a mark. Ticks can carry diseases, so an adult should remove one carefully.
fact: A tick can be a mark (✓) that shows something is right or done. Americans usually call it a check mark.
fact: A tick is also the short sound a clock makes each second, so a clock makes 60 ticks in a minute.
fact: A tick is a tiny creature with eight legs. It bites animals and people and sucks their blood.
fact: To tick means to make a tick mark, or to make the ticking sound. «In a tick» is British and means in a moment.
fact: «A jiffy», «a tick», «a mo» and «two shakes» all mean a short moment, so the same idea can come from different words.
exercise: «The teacher put a tick next to each right answer.» What does tick mean here? | *A mark that shows an answer is right | A tiny creature that bites | To run very fast | A short sound, like a clock
exercise: «Ticks live in long grass, so check your skin after a walk.» What is a tick here? | A moment of time | A mark on a test | A clock sound | *A tiny creature with eight legs
exercise: Jayden says, «Back in a tick!» What does he mean? | *He will be back in a moment | He will be back in one hundred years | He is a tiny creature that bites | He will not come back at the end of the lesson
test: «The clock went tick, tick, tick all through the maths lesson.» What is the tick here? | *The short sound a clock makes each second | A tiny creature in the grass | A mark for a right answer | To tick a box on a form
test: «Please tick the box if you want a drink.» What does tick mean here? | To make the ticking sound of a clock | To run away quickly | To bite and suck blood | *To make a tick mark to show your choice
exam: Ella says, «Wait a tick, I am nearly done.» Which word means the same as tick here? | A sound | A creature | *A moment | A mark
